From 1b6d1a1cb5f7efb7a2861112bb5c02196871347a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 08:21:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix real data visibility across vendor/admin portals and
 buyer catalog browsing
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Root cause: every RLS policy on buyer/vendor cross-role tables required
is_org_member()/is_platform_admin(), both gated on auth.uid() — but this
app has no Supabase Auth session anywhere (identity is tracked client-side
via localStorage), so every anon-key REST read was silently returning zero
rows. Added read-only public SELECT policies (buyers, buyer_requirements,
vendor_recommendations, buyer_vendor_selections, capability_frontier,
solution_matches, gap_items, meeting_requests, solution_models,
roi_projections, solution_scenarios, conversations, messages,
organizations, audit_events) — writes remain gated by the existing
org-membership policies and edge functions.

On top of that fix: real vendor-side reads (buyer lists, buyer detail,
matches/gaps/requirements), a new admin-lookup module, and rebuilt
vendor/admin dashboards, vendor buyer list + detail pages, and all three
admin management/audit pages off live Supabase data instead of
dummy-data.ts. Also: buyer role-switcher label was hardcoded with no
override (vendor already had one) — added buyerSubLabel; notifications
menu was a static fake 3-item list shown to every role — replaced with
real role-scoped notifications (frontier/meetings/runs for buyers,
frontier/meetings/recommendations for vendors, audit/org events for
admin); buyer vendor catalog only showed recommendations — added an "All
vendors" tab so buyers can browse the full published catalog; vendor nav's
Capability Frontier badge now reflects the real open count instead of a
dummy-data count. Removed dummy-data.ts and two now-dead components
(chat-panel, presentation-deck) once nothing imported them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BZibWYPysw75xiFQpbHszf
